# GitHub linguist setup for Luau-first repo
**/*.lua linguist-language=Lua

# Treat non-Luau tooling as vendored
**/*.js linguist-vendored
**/*.ts linguist-vendored
**/*.sh linguist-vendored
**/*.ps1 linguist-vendored
**/*.bat linguist-vendored
**/*.json linguist-vendored
**/*.yml linguist-vendored
**/*.yaml linguist-vendored
**/*.md linguist-vendored

# Tool directories
tools/** linguist-vendored
scripts/** linguist-vendored

# Line endings are FROZEN AS STORED. Do not remove this.
#
# `core.autocrlf` is true on a lot of Windows machines, including the one this
# repo is usually built on, and it converts line endings on checkout. That made
# a working copy of src/lucide-icons-data.lua end CRLF while the blob in git
# ended LF -- and git reported the file as CLEAN, because its stat cache
# matched and it never re-read the contents.
#
# The monolith built from that working copy therefore differed by one byte from
# the monolith anyone else builds, and the reproducibility gate failed in CI
# with a diff nobody could reproduce locally. The build cannot be deterministic
# while a checkout can quietly change the bytes it reads.
#
# -text means: store what you are given, hand back exactly that, on every
# platform. It changes no file's content, only git's meddling.
* -text
